Subject: [PATCH 33/44] recipe: image input is supported, with the numbers
 behind it

Rewrites the Images section so it stands alone: what the tower is and the one
field it differs in, the conversion detail that decides working from failing,
how to serve it, the parity numbers against the model's own bf16 noise floor
with all 27 blocks checked, what it reads and the one thing it does not, perf
with an image, and the tower's default-init trap for anyone adding a dump.

Measured, not estimated: tower engine-vs-bf16 max 3.63 cos 0.99869 inside a
3.86 / 0.99784 noise floor; 513 of 513 M-RoPE cells; seven benchmark labels
read correctly; 164 prompt tokens at 1397-1519 tok/s prefill and 30.7 tok/s
decode. Text-only numbers are unchanged, so the page keeps one set of perf
figures and adds vision beside them.
